id: pm-geywoc
title: Redact sensitive values in Sentry command context and encoded diagnostic text
description: "sentrySetCommandContext currently preserves every non-option argument verbatim, including free text and space-separated option values. Broader successful-command tracing must use safe argument structure and streamed-span/log scrubbing through the existing policy instead of collecting private item content."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: bugfix,observability,privacy,sdk,security
created_at: "2026-10-13T04:41:25.527Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-14T21:03:59.047Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-14T21:03:57.632Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-14T21:03:57.632Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "Positional content and separate option values never enter Sentry context or breadcrumbs; streamed spans and logs scrub sensitive data before export; independent negative controls fail before the fix and pass after; existing error classification and consent remain intact.; Quoted sensitive keys, Unicode delimiters and separators, serialized JSON, and nested containers are redacted at registered hooks and real loopback export; Opaque encoded boundaries fail closed while safe controls, typed attributes, caller scope and linear scanning remain intact; Exact candidate Node and Bun acceptance requires a complete privacy case inventory and retained digests"
parent: pm-5oj5
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: "Keep character and encoding width in each sensitive container boundary, rejecting malformed escaped and Unicode-encoded closers without exposing remaining values. Retain prior quoted-key, Unicode, scope, consent and final-envelope protections and require35 installed-consumer cases."
expected_result: "Synthetic sensitive markers do not survive event, streamed-span or log serialization, including malformed escaped/encoded container boundaries, while safe controls and caller scope remain intact."
actual_result: The new35-case loopback consumer fails before the fix at escaped-container-close and passes after. Native linked run test-local-mv8l8e8r-61jpg3 passes all3 selected commands and records required_privacy_cases35 at threshold35; current compiled public SDK passes under Node and Bun. Existing unit and integration checks pass after raising the explicit inventory assertion from33 to35. A fresh whole-source exact coverage run is active; exact revised-head hosted coverage/static/smoke/review are required before merge. Published14 remains the original failing baseline; no second same-day pm-cli version or policy relaxation introduced.
affected_version: 2026.10.14
